[[{"text": "NSW HSC 4 Unit Mathematics Examination 1983", "x0": 0.26043956043956046, "y0": 0.11655011655011654, "x1": 0.7703296703296704, "y1": 0.12665112665112666}, {"text": "1. (i) Draw a careful sketch of the curve y = indicating clearly any vertical", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.1522921522921523, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.16705516705516704}, {"text": "or horizontal asymptotes, turning points or inflexions.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.17016317016317017, "x1": 0.621978021978022, "y1": 0.18337218337218336}, {"text": "(ii) A function f(r) is known to approach 0 as x appoaches oo and \u2014oo. Its derivative", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.19658119658119658, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.2097902097902098}, {"text": "is given by (x \u2014", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.21522921522921523, "x1": 0.3989010989010989, "y1": 0.22921522921522922}, {"text": "From this information, describe the behaviour of f(x) as a increases from \u2014co to", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.24164724164724163, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.2556332556332556}, {"text": "+00. Include in your description an indication of those \u00ab where f(x) is respectively", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.2595182595182595, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.2727272727272727}, {"text": "increasing or decreasing and any points where f has a maximum or minimum value.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.2766122766122766, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.2898212898212898}, {"text": "Also explain why f(x) must be positive for all real x.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.29292929292929293, "x1": 0.6175824175824176, "y1": 0.30691530691530694}, {"text": "Draw a sketch of a function f(x", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.3201243201243201, "x1": 0.42967032967032964, "y1": 0.3333333333333333}, {"text": "tisfying the given conditions.", "x0": 0.46373626373626375, "y0": 0.3201243201243201, "x1": 0.710989010989011, "y1": 0.3333333333333333}, {"text": "2. (i) Find: (a) 22 de (b) 602\u00b0(1 + dr", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.35586635586635584, "x1": 0.6934065934065934, "y1": 0.37218337218337216}, {"text": "(c) fy ve~/) dx, where T is a positive number.", "x0": 0.26703296703296703, "y0": 0.3853923853923854, "x1": 0.7021978021978021, "y1": 0.4048174048174048}, {"text": "16x", "x0": 0.6395604395604395, "y0": 0.4156954156954157, "x1": 0.6626373626373626, "y1": 0.4226884226884227}, {"text": "Hence show that", "x0": 0.7175824175824176, "y0": 0.41802641802641805, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.4281274281274281}, {"text": "(ii) Find the partial fraction decomposition of", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.41802641802641805, "x1": 0.610989010989011, "y1": 0.43123543123543123}, {"text": "Pst", "x0": 0.6285714285714286, "y0": 0.4257964257964258, "x1": 0.6802197802197802, "y1": 0.43278943278943277}, {"text": "Je der = log, (4/3), and also evaluate J) dz.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.43512043512043513, "x1": 0.6351648351648351, "y1": 0.4553224553224553}, {"text": "s60 + isin6@ =", "x0": 0.7406593406593407, "y0": 0.4763014763014763, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.48717948717948717}, {"text": "3. Use mathematical induction to prove that for any real", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.4763014763014763, "x1": 0.6879120879120879, "y1": 0.48951048951048953}, {"text": "(cos 6 + isin", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.4933954933954934, "x1": 0.2571428571428571, "y1": 0.5066045066045066}, {"text": "Find the six sixth roots of \u20141, expressing each in the form \u00ab + iy with real.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.5198135198135199, "x1": 0.8516483516483516, "y1": 0.533022533022533}, {"text": "4", "x0": 0.510989010989011, "y0": 0.5446775446775447, "x1": 0.5175824175824176, "y1": 0.5516705516705517}, {"text": "Find also the four roots of the equation z4\u2014 2? + 1 = 0, and indicate their positions", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.5446775446775447, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.5602175602175602}, {"text": "on an Argand diagram.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.5633255633255633, "x1": 0.35274725274725277, "y1": 0.5765345765345765}, {"text": "4. (i) Determine the (real) values of A for which the equation =; + 3", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.5912975912975913, "x1": 0.7538461538461538, "y1": 0.6177156177156177}, {"text": "= 1 defines", "x0": 0.7857142857142857, "y0": 0.5998445998445998, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.60994560994561}, {"text": "respectively an ellipse and an hyperbola.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.6177156177156177, "x1": 0.5054945054945055, "y1": 0.6309246309246309}, {"text": "Sketch the curve corresponding to the value \\ = 1.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.6441336441336442, "x1": 0.5945054945054945, "y1": 0.6573426573426573}, {"text": "Describe how the shape of this curve changes as \\ increases from 1 towards 2. What", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.6705516705516705, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.6837606837606838}, {"text": "is the limiting position of the curve as 2 is approached?", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.6876456876456877, "x1": 0.6362637362637362, "y1": 0.7008547008547008}, {"text": "(ii) P is a point on the ellipse % = 1 with centre O. A line drawn from O,", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.7117327117327117, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.7319347319347319}, {"text": "parallel to the tangent to the ellipse at P, meets the ellipse at Q", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7334887334887334, "x1": 0.7164835164835165, "y1": 0.7466977466977467}, {"text": "Prrove that the area of the triangle OPQ is independent of the position of P.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7606837606837606, "x1": 0.8274725274725274, "y1": 0.7738927738927739}, {"text": "5. (i) An egg-timer has the shape of an hour-glass and can be described mathe-", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7956487956487956, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.8096348096348096}, {"text": "matically as being obtained by rotating the curve y = x + 623, -1/V2 < x < 1/Vv2,", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.811965811965812, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.8275058275058275}, {"text": "about the y-axis.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.8313908313908314, "x1": 0.2967032967032967, "y1": 0.8445998445998446}, {"text": "Use the method of decomposition into cylindrical shells to calculate its volume,", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.8585858585858586, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.8717948717948718}, {"text": "correct to three significant figures.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.8756798756798757, "x1": 0.44945054945054946, "y1": 0.8888888888888888}], [{"text": "(ii) A plane curve is defined implicitly by the equation x? + ry +y\u00b0 =4.", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.11421911421911422, "x1": 0.8010989010989011, "y1": 0.12975912975912976}, {"text": "This curve has a horizontal tangent at the point Show that X is the unique", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.14219114219114218, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.1554001554001554}, {"text": "real root of the equation X\u00b0 + X?+4=0, and that <-1", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.15695415695415696, "x1": 0.7373626373626374, "y1": 0.17249417249417248}, {"text": "6. An object of irregular shape and of mass 100 kilograms is found to experience", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.19347319347319347, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.2066822066822067}, {"text": "a resistive force, in newtons, of magnitude one-tenth the square of its velocity in", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.21056721056721056, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.22377622377622378}, {"text": "metres per second when it moves through the air.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.22688422688422688, "x1": 0.5846153846153846, "y1": 0.2400932400932401}, {"text": "If the object falls from rest under gravity, assumed constant of value 9.8 m.s", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.25252525252525254, "x1": 0.8527472527472527, "y1": 0.26573426573426573}, {"text": "calculate", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.26961926961926963, "x1": 0.22637362637362637, "y1": 0.27972027972027974}, {"text": "(i) its terminal velocity:", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.29448329448329447, "x1": 0.36043956043956044, "y1": 0.3084693084693085}, {"text": "(ii) the minimum height, to the nearest metre, of the release point above ground, if", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.3209013209013209, "x1": 0.8824175824175824, "y1": 0.3341103341103341}, {"text": "it attains a speed of 80% of its terminal velocity before striking the ground.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.3372183372183372, "x1": 0.8142857142857143, "y1": 0.35120435120435123}, {"text": "7. (i) A city council consists of 6 Liberal and 5 Labor aldermen, from whom a", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.3714063714063714, "x1": 0.8813186813186813, "y1": 0.3853923853923854}, {"text": "committee of 5 members is chosen at random. What is the probability that the", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.38927738927738925, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.4024864024864025}, {"text": "Liberals have a majority on the committee?", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.4063714063714064, "x1": 0.5340659340659341, "y1": 0.4195804195804196}, {"text": "(ii) Let a, 6,7 be the roots of the equation x? +x +r where r #0. Obtain as", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.4296814296814297, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.4444444444444444}, {"text": "functions of q,r in their simplest forms, the coefficients of the cubic equations whose", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.4483294483294483, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.46153846153846156}, {"text": "roots are:", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.466977466977467, "x1": 0.22747252747252747, "y1": 0.4755244755244755}, {"text": "(a) a? 9s (b) (c)", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.48951048951048953, "x1": 0.6065934065934065, "y1": 0.5050505050505051}, {"text": "(iii) Given that \u00ab + y = s, prove that, for x > 0,y >0,s >0, 2+ > 4, and that", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.5151515151515151, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.5314685314685315}, {"text": "&", "x0": 0.24615384615384617, "y0": 0.5353535353535354, "x1": 0.26153846153846155, "y1": 0.5439005439005439}, {"text": "iny = A \u2014 cos B), find A, B in terms of x, y. Hence prove", "x0": 0.3241758241758242, "y0": 0.5633255633255633, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.5889665889665889}, {"text": "that for any positive integer n,", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.5881895881895882, "x1": 0.4186813186813187, "y1": 0.6013986013986014}, {"text": "sing +sin3x +--+ +sin(2n \u20141)x", "x0": 0.25934065934065936, "y0": 0.6223776223776224, "x1": 0.6263736263736264, "y1": 0.6355866355866356}, {"text": "(ii) In a triangle ABC, the point X on BC is such that AX bisects ZBAC. Use", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.6643356643356644, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.6775446775446775}, {"text": "the sine rule to prove that AB/AC = BX/XC.", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.6806526806526807, "x1": 0.5615384615384615, "y1": 0.6946386946386947}, {"text": "In the figure, XY represents a vertical", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7156177156177156, "x1": 0.4879120879120879, "y1": 0.7288267288267288}, {"text": "flagstaff of length a placed on top of a", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7327117327117327, "x1": 0.4846153846153846, "y1": 0.745920745920746}, {"text": "vertical tower AY of height b. An observer", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7498057498057498, "x1": 0.5252747252747253, "y1": 0.763014763014763}, {"text": "is at a point O, which is a vertical height h", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7668997668997669, "x1": 0.5274725274725275, "y1": 0.7801087801087802}, {"text": "above B, and a horizontal distance d from", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.7839937839937839, "x1": 0.5208791208791209, "y1": 0.7964257964257965}, {"text": "A. Given that ZXOY = ZYOA, show that", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.8010878010878011, "x1": 0.5318681318681319, "y1": 0.8135198135198135}, {"text": "(a \u2014b)d? = (a + b)b \u2014 26h \u2014 (a \u2014 b)h?. A", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.8158508158508159, "x1": 0.5472527472527473, "y1": 0.8430458430458431}]]